{"nodes": [{"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide", "label": "Architecture Guide", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide_architectural_style_selection", "label": "Architectural Style Selection Matrix", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": "Architectural Style Selection", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each style is paired with an explicit Avoid When column - modular monolith fails when independent per-module scaling is needed, microservices when the team is small, event-driven when strong consistency is required everywhere - so selection is driven by system characteristics rather than fashion."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide_component_boundary_identification", "label": "Component Boundary Identification", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": "Component Boundary Identification", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A boundary is correct when the component has one nameable responsibility, owns its data, absorbs internal change without ripple, tests in isolation, and exposes a clear public API. Red flags: components that always deploy together, circular dependencies, pass-through proxies, and shared tables written by multiple components."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide_design_pattern_checklist", "label": "Design Pattern Checklist", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": "Design Pattern Checklist", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four gates per pattern decision: problem fit (a specific problem, not a hypothetical one), complexity cost, team familiarity without the architect present, and testing impact. Repository, CQRS, Saga, Strategy, and Adapter each carry a stated when-to-use."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide_adr_format", "label": "ADR Format (Architecture Guide)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": "ADR Format", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide_infrastructure_pattern_alignment", "label": "Infrastructure Pattern Alignment", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": "Infrastructure Pattern Alignment", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Application topology must be validated against infrastructure reality: stateless services scale horizontally, stateful ones need sticky sessions or distributed cache, background workers must be queue-driven and idempotent with dead-letter handling, scheduled jobs must handle overlapping executions, edge functions cannot hold persistent connections."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide_reverse_engineering_synthesis_checklist", "label": "Reverse Engineering Synthesis Checklist", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": "Reverse Engineering Synthesis Checklist", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eight ordered steps applied to Developer code-scan results: identify the dominant style or its absence, map components to bounded contexts, trace data flow, flag coupling hotspots by fan-in/fan-out, find missing boundaries (god classes, shared state), check test coverage against architectural risk, contrast observed with intended patterns, and emit a component inventory rated healthy/at-risk/degraded."}], "edges": [{"source": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide", "target": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide_architectural_style_selection", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": "Architectural Style Selection", "weight": 1}, {"source": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide", "target": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide_component_boundary_identification", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": "Component Boundary Identification", "weight": 1}, {"source": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide", "target": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide_design_pattern_checklist", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": "Design Pattern Checklist", "weight": 1}, {"source": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide", "target": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide_adr_format", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/architecture-guide.md", "source_location": "ADR Format", "weight": 1}, {"source": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide", "target": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_architecture_guide